  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe designMode setter currently says:\n\n>2. If value is \"on\" and [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)'s [design mode enabled](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#design-mode-enabled) is false:\n> …\n>    3. Run the [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focusing-steps) for [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)'s [document element](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element), if non-null.\n\ni.e. setting designMode synchronously blurs the focused element. However, in practice in all browsers, if the focused element is in a shadow root, then it's not blurred (since design mode doesn't go through shadow roots). So maybe the wording of this step should be reconsidered.\n\nExample:\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<div><template shadowrootmode=\"open\"><a href=\"#\">link</a></template></div>\n<script>\ndocument.querySelector(\"div\").shadowRoot.querySelector(\"a\").focus();\ndocument.designMode = \"on\";\n</script>\n```",
